terval can be represented by the following inequality:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,4\n$$\n\nWe can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\in [2,4)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdf77469-6c2a-5339-b216-3bc5e2316e4d" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Between Half-Open Intervals and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38fce6e7-e608-5049-89bd-6546b8fda8e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<y\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482909} {:answer/id #uuid "43f5ec63-ec14-578f-9c9b-502470b6d4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482929} {:answer/id #uuid "6315912c-de0b-5577-9bf6-3e2c64fe43c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482985} {:answer/id #uuid "631761de-21bd-51da-88ac-879266e500a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482986} {:answer/id #uuid "d1720d90-8cb3-5638-bf04-aaa94a4aeaba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1720d90-8cb3-5638-bf04-aaa94a4aeaba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483161} :answer-field/id #uuid "d78e9d72-459d-5fce-90e1-8180676b9ebb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8242dd7c-9e76-5a08-b5a0-1fe98445b603" :question/math-academy-id "q-73902" :question/problem "The interval $y\\in [-1,2)$ corresponds to the inequality" :question/worked-solution "Every interval can be expressed as an inequality. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ to indicate that the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ to indicate that the endpoints *are* included.\n\nFor the given interval \n\n$$\n[-1,2\\,)\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $-1$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $\\le \\,.$\n\n- The right endpoint $2$ is *not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $<\\,.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality that corresponds to the given interval is \n\n$$\n-1\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,y\\,\\,<\\,\\,2.\n$$"}]}
